from __future__ import annotations

NAME = "The Garden of Tranquility"
AMBIENCE = "Wind in Pines"

# A soothing sleep-lecture about Epicurean tranquility -- ataraxia, simple pleasures already near, wanting little, the quiet friendship of the garden.
SECTIONS = [['You are lying down now, and there is nothing left to do tonight.', 'Let your body grow heavy against the bed, sinking just a little deeper with each breath.', 'Breathe in slowly, gently, and let the breath go without any effort at all.', 'There is no hurry here, and there is nowhere else you need to be.', 'Imagine a quiet walled garden at dusk, its gate softly closed behind you.', 'The air is warm and still, and the light is fading into a soft and kindly blue.', 'You can feel the cool earth beneath your feet and the calm of an evening settling all around.', 'Somewhere nearby, leaves stir, and then they are still again.', 'Let your shoulders soften, let your jaw loosen, let your hands lie open and at rest.', 'With every breath out, a little more of the day drifts away from you.', 'You are safe inside these quiet walls, and the evening is yours to rest in.', 'Let yourself settle here, slowly, gently, as the garden grows dim and peaceful.'], ['In a garden much like this one, long ago, an old teacher gathered his friends at the close of the day.', 'He did not ask them to be clever, or busy, or anything other than what they were.', 'He believed that the truest sweetness in life is a calm and untroubled mind.', 'Not riches, he would say softly, and not fame, but a heart at peace with itself.', 'He called this gentle calm the deepest happiness a person can know.', 'And he noticed that it does not come from far away, but settles quietly when the striving stops.', 'Tonight you need not chase it, for it is already drifting toward you.', 'Feel how your mind grows still, the way the garden grows still at dusk.', 'There is nothing to solve and nothing to win in this quiet hour.', 'An untroubled mind, the old teacher taught, is its own soft reward.', 'Let that calm spread through you now, slow and warm and unhurried.', 'You are simply here, breathing, and that is more than enough.'], ['The philosophers of the garden taught that the deepest pleasures are simple ones.', 'They are not rare or distant, but already near, already within reach.', 'Think of the warmth of a bed when you are tired, and how gladly the body sinks into it.', 'Think of water when you are thirsty, and how it is sweeter than any wine.', 'Think of bread when you are hungry, and the quiet contentment of a belly that is full.', 'These are the small joys the old teacher loved, and he found them more than enough.', 'You have such gifts around you tonight, simple and plain and kind.', 'A soft place to rest, a quiet room, the gentle weight of a blanket.', 'There is no luxury you are lacking in this moment, nothing missing at all.', 'The simplest comforts are the ones that last, and you are wrapped in them now.', 'Let yourself feel how richly you are cared for by these small and ordinary things.', 'Breathe, and be glad of the plain sweetness that is already here.'], ['The old teacher knew that we carry many fears, and most of them are heavier than they need to be.', 'He taught his friends that fears grow large in the mind but stay small in the world.', 'When you look at a worry gently, without struggling against it, it begins to soften.', 'Most of the things we dread never arrive, and most that do are gentler than we feared.', 'So let your fears rest at the gate tonight, for they cannot follow you into sleep.', 'The cravings that pull at us, he said, are much the same, larger in longing than in truth.', 'When you want a little less, you find that you already have a great deal.', 'Notice how, right now, there is nothing you truly need that you do not already hold.', 'The wanting quiets, the fearing quiets, and a deep stillness opens in their place.', 'You can set down the heavy things now, one by one, and feel how light you become.', 'Looked at kindly, the night holds no threat, only its soft and patient dark.', 'Let the fears grow small, and let the calm grow wide.'], ['To want little, the philosophers of the garden taught, is to be quietly rich.', 'And to be content with what you have is a kind of freedom that nothing can take.', 'The one who needs only a little is never poor, for enough is always within reach.', 'Tonight you have enough, more than enough, and enough is a feast.', 'A warm bed, a safe room, the slow and steady rhythm of your breath.', 'What more could this gentle hour ask of you than to rest in it?', 'The old teacher counted himself wealthy on bread and water and the company of friends.', 'He found a feast in the plainest meal when his heart was calm and his mind was free.', 'You too are wealthy tonight, in all the ways that truly matter.', 'Let contentment fill you the way evening fills a quiet garden.', 'There is nothing to add and nothing to take away, only enough, and enough is plenty.', 'Rest in that richness now, easy and free and untroubled.'], ['In the garden, the old teacher gathered friends, and friendship was its own deep pleasure.', 'Here no one needed to prove anything, or to be more than they were.', 'Among true friends you can simply be yourself, and that is rest enough for the soul.', 'Imagine such gentle company around you now, asking nothing, only glad you are near.', 'The quiet friendship of the garden asks for no performance and keeps no account.', 'He taught that the bonds of kindness are among the sweetest things a life can hold.', 'You are held in that same warmth tonight, safe among unseen friends.', 'And should some small pain come, the old teacher said, it is usually brief or bearable.', 'Sharp pain does not last long, and lasting aches are gentle enough to carry.', 'But this night holds none of it, no ache and no trouble, only rest.', 'There is nothing to brace against in this soft and quiet dark.', 'You are at ease here, untroubled, among friends, with nothing left to prove.'], ['Now let the garden grow dim, and let yourself grow dimmer with it.', 'There is nothing you want, nothing you fear, nothing you must do.', 'The gate is closed, the walls are kind, and the evening holds you gently.', 'Your breath is slow, your body is heavy, your mind is quiet and clear.', 'You have enough tonight, and enough is a feast, and the feast is over now.', 'Let your thoughts drift like leaves settling softly onto cool dark ground.', 'Each breath out carries you a little deeper into the peace of the garden.', 'There is no striving here, no longing, only the calm of being at rest.', 'You are untroubled, you are content, you are free, and you are safe.', 'Let the stillness take you, slowly, sweetly, with no need to hold on.', 'Rest now in the quiet garden, wanting nothing, at peace with everything.', 'Sleep, gently, and let the calm carry you all the way down.']]
